          "id": "code-ml-09-1-ch09_1_diag",
          "title": "Diagnostik Empiris Fungsi Varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p (Taylor Power Law)",
          "language": "python",
          "filename": "09_1_variance_power_diagnostic.py",
          "code": "import numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import TweedieRegressor\n\ndef estimate_variance_power(y: np.ndarray, mu_hat: np.ndarray, n_bins: int = 8) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Estimasi empiris pangkat p pada fungsi varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p (Taylor Power Law).\"\"\"\n    edges = np.quantile(mu_hat, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1))\n    bin_means, bin_vars = [], []\n    for k in range(n_bins):\n        lo, hi = edges[k], edges[k + 1]\n        mask = (mu_hat >= lo) & (mu_hat <= hi if k == n_bins - 1 else mu_hat < hi)\n        if np.sum(mask) < 25:\n            continue\n        m_k = float(np.mean(mu_hat[mask]))\n        # Varians residual empiris di dalam bin k\n        v_k = float(np.var(y[mask] - mu_hat[mask], ddof=1))\n        if m_k > 1e-6 and v_k > 1e-8:\n            bin_means.append(m_k)\n            bin_vars.append(v_k)\n    log_m = np.log(np.array(bin_means))\n    log_v = np.log(np.array(bin_vars))\n    slope_p, intercept_log_phi = np.polyfit(log_m, log_v, 1)\n    return float(slope_p), float(np.exp(intercept_log_phi))\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\nn = 1500\nX = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(n, 2))\neta = 2.0 + 0.6 * X[:, 0] - 0.5 * X[:, 1]\nmu_true = np.exp(eta)\n\n# Bangkitkan 4 dataset dengan fungsi varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p yang berbeda\ny_p0 = mu_true + rng.normal(0.0, 1.8, size=n)                    # Normal: p = 0, phi = 3.24\ny_p1 = rng.poisson(mu_true).astype(float)                        # Poisson: p = 1, phi = 1.00\n# Compound Poisson-Gamma dengan shape alpha=1 -> p = (alpha+2)/(alpha+1) = 1.5\nlam_cp = (mu_true ** 0.5) / (1.2 * 0.5)\nn_claims = rng.poisson(lam_cp)\ny_p15 = np.array([rng.gamma(1.0, 1.2 * 0.5 * (mu_true[i] ** 0.5), size=n_claims[i]).sum() if n_claims[i] > 0 else 0.0 for i in range(n)])\ny_p2 = rng.gamma(shape=4.0, scale=mu_true / 4.0)                 # Gamma: p = 2, phi = 0.25\n\nprint(\"=== Audit Otomatis Fungsi Varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p (Log-Var vs Log-Mean) ===\")\nprint(\"Distribusi Sejati          | p Sejati | p Estimasi | phi Estimasi | Rekomendasi GLM\")\nprint(\"-\" * 86)\ncases = [\n    (\"Normal (Homoskedastik)   \", 0.0, y_p0, 0.0),\n    (\"Poisson (Count Data)     \", 1.0, y_p1, 1.0),\n    (\"Tweedie Compound (p=1.5) \", 1.5, y_p15, 1.5),\n    (\"Gamma (Constant CV)      \", 2.0, y_p2, 2.0),\n]\nfor name, p_true, y_obs, fit_p in cases:\n    link = \"identity\" if fit_p == 0.0 else \"log\"\n    mdl = TweedieRegressor(power=fit_p, link=link, alpha=0.0).fit(X, y_obs)\n    mu_hat = np.maximum(mdl.predict(X), 1e-4)\n    p_est, phi_est = estimate_variance_power(y_obs, mu_hat, n_bins=8)\n    if p_est < 0.45:\n        rec = \"Normal / OLS\"\n    elif p_est < 1.25:\n        rec = \"Poisson / NB\"\n    elif p_est < 1.75:\n        rec = \"Tweedie (1<p<2)\"\n    else:\n        rec = \"Gamma (p=2)\"\n    print(f\"{name:26s} | {p_true:8.2f} | {p_est:10.3f} | {phi_est:12.3f} | {rec}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== Audit Otomatis Fungsi Varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p (Log-Var vs Log-Mean) ===\nDistribusi Sejati          | p Sejati | p Estimasi | phi Estimasi | Rekomendasi GLM\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNormal (Homoskedastik)     |     0.00 |      0.214 |        3.553 | Normal / OLS\nPoisson (Count Data)       |     1.00 |      1.067 |        0.869 | Poisson / NB\nTweedie Compound (p=1.5)   |     1.50 |      1.508 |        1.169 | Tweedie (1<p<2)\nGamma (Constant CV)        |     2.00 |      2.166 |        0.200 | Gamma (p=2)",
          "actualOutput": "=== Audit Otomatis Fungsi Varians V(mu) = phi * mu^p (Log-Var vs Log-Mean) ===\nDistribusi Sejati          | p Sejati | p Estimasi | phi Estimasi | Rekomendasi GLM\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNormal (Homoskedastik)     |     0.00 |      0.214 |        3.553 | Normal / OLS\nPoisson (Count Data)       |     1.00 |      1.067 |        0.869 | Poisson / NB\nTweedie Compound (p=1.5)   |     1.50 |      1.508 |        1.169 | Tweedie (1<p<2)\nGamma (Constant CV)        |     2.00 |      2.166 |        0.200 | Gamma (p=2)",
          "explanation": "Mengestimasi eksponen varians p secara otomatis melalui regresi log-varians terhadap log-mean antar kuantil untuk membedakan Normal, Poisson, Tweedie, dan Gamma.",
