          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef tweedie_d2_and_ae_ratio(y_true, y_pred, power: float = 1.5, sample_weight=None) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    y = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=float)\n    mu = np.asarray(y_pred, dtype=float)\n    w = np.ones_like(y) if sample_weight is None else np.asarray(sample_weight, dtype=float)\n    def unit_dev(yt, mt):\n        t1 = np.where(yt > 0.0, (yt ** (2.0 - power)) / ((1.0 - power) * (2.0 - power)), 0.0)\n        t2 = (yt * (mt ** (1.0 - power))) / (1.0 - power)\n        t3 = (mt ** (2.0 - power)) / (2.0 - power)\n        return 2.0 * (t1 - t2 + t3)\n    y_bar = float(np.sum(w * y) / np.sum(w))\n    d_mod = float(np.sum(w * unit_dev(y, mu)))\n    d_null = float(np.sum(w * unit_dev(y, np.full_like(y, y_bar))))\n    d2 = 1.0 - d_mod / d_null\n    ae = float(np.sum(w * y) / np.sum(w * mu))\n    return (round(d2, 4), round(ae, 4))\n```"
